=== Phase G: Agent App Beta knowledge scenario - FAIL (release-blocking) ===
date: 2026-08-12T06:45:43Z

## Finding
Binding a knowledge set to a roster Agent and running a chat fails with:
  CompositorSessionSnapshot layer names must match compositor layers in order.
  Expected [agent_app_user_prompt, execution_context, shell, config, history, llm, knowledge],
  got [agent_app_user_prompt, execution_context, shell, config, history, llm].
Source: dify_agent.runtime.runner.AgentRunValidationError (agent_backend),
  agenton/compositor/core.py:314 _validate_session_snapshot.

## Repro
1. PUT /agent/{id}/composer with agent_soul.knowledge.sets=[{dataset}] -> 200 (save OK)
2. POST /agent/{id}/publish -> success
3. POST /agent/{id}/chat-messages (knowledge question) -> 400 completion_request_error
   Agent backend: layer mismatch (knowledge layer missing from session snapshot)

## Impact
Agent App Beta knowledge retrieval scenario FAILS. Without knowledge binding the same
chat works (PhaseG-OK PASS). With knowledge bound, every conversation 400s.
Blocks release: VALIDATION_PLAN Agent knowledge scenario cannot pass.

## Note
This is a runtime integration bug between the API's runtime_request_builder and the
agenton compositor; not an environment artifact.
